# Vercel uploads everything that is not ignored, and .vercelignore excludes files
# from the deployment upload — so anything listed here simply does not exist at build time.
#
# This file used to allowlist-by-exclusion and accidentally listed live app routes
# (src/app/cards, src/app/sets, src/app/wiki, src/app/collection, src/app/decks,
# src/app/packs, src/app/releases, src/app/search, src/app/fan-art) plus
# public/panther.glb and public/panther-meshy-8192.jpg, which were tracked and rendered
# by the app. Those pages 404'd and the hero 3D/textures 404'd on every deploy.
#
# It is now inverted to an allowlist: ignore the repo root, then opt the build inputs in.
# That keeps the ~300MB of root-level scratch (renders, .zip dumps, sample .glb/.obj)
# out of the upload without ever dropping a route again.
#
# NOTE: if you add a NEW root-level build input (middleware.ts, vercel.json,
# instrumentation.ts, custom tsconfig-like config...), allowlist it below or Vercel
# will not upload it and the build will fail or behave differently from local.

# Ignore everything at the repo root (non-recursive: subdirs are opted in below).
/*

# App source + static assets
!/src
!/public

# Build inputs
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/next.config.ts
!/tsconfig.json
!/postcss.config.mjs
!/eslint.config.mjs

# Never uploaded, whatever else changes:
node_modules
.next
out
.netlify
.vercel
.git
*.log
.env*
